WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.799
[moody, intense intro music plays]

01:06.066 --> 01:07.609
[girl breathing heavily]

01:14.532 --> 01:16.284
AGE RANGE FOR JUVENILE ACT

01:16.367 --> 01:18.369
[continues breathing heavily]

01:29.214 --> 01:32.425
[Dong-eun] Once upon a time,
I entertained this thought.

01:38.181 --> 01:41.101
[GPS] You have now reached
your destination.

01:41.601 --> 01:43.645
-[clattering]
-[man] What'd you do wrong? Answer!

01:43.728 --> 01:45.897
What'd you do wrong?
Answer, you fucking bitch!

01:45.980 --> 01:47.649
Fucking disrespect me again…

01:47.732 --> 01:49.818
[Dong-eun] What if somebody, anybody,

01:50.777 --> 01:52.278
had tried to come and help me?

01:52.362 --> 01:53.446
[man] Goddamn woman.

01:57.117 --> 01:59.202
-[man] Where're you going?
-[woman] No!

01:59.285 --> 02:00.370
[woman wails]

02:00.453 --> 02:03.748
[man] Think anyone's going to help you?
Think you can get away from me?

02:03.832 --> 02:06.084
That's it. You're gonna die now!

02:07.001 --> 02:08.086
Don't hit her!

02:08.670 --> 02:10.839
Please! I'm going to fucking kill you
if you don't stop!

02:10.922 --> 02:13.466
Seon-a, please don't. Don't do it.

02:13.550 --> 02:16.344
Please. Your mom…
Your mom's taking care of it.

02:16.427 --> 02:19.848
-Seon-a, I'm begging you.
-No, Mom, I have to! I have to, Mom!

02:19.931 --> 02:22.684
You'll get arrested if you do it,
but I'll be fine 'cause I'm a minor.

02:22.767 --> 02:26.020
-So move, please!
-Please don't do this! Don't!

02:26.104 --> 02:26.938
[mother sobbing]

02:27.021 --> 02:29.858
If I have to… I'll do it.
You shouldn't have to!

02:29.941 --> 02:30.900
Seon-a…

02:31.401 --> 02:32.610
Please, stop.

02:32.694 --> 02:34.946
You two bitches
have lost your goddamn mind!

02:35.029 --> 02:37.699
-[wails]
-Such a good role model, aren't you?

02:37.782 --> 02:40.368
Such a good role model!
The greatest role model!

02:40.952 --> 02:43.705
Fucking whore. I think you need
another beating, don't you?

02:44.789 --> 02:47.834
Are you going to stab me with that, huh?

02:48.585 --> 02:50.295
Huh?! Then stab me.

02:50.378 --> 02:52.505
Stab me! You stupid bitch.

02:53.381 --> 02:55.300
You guys are out of you fucking minds.

02:56.176 --> 02:58.678
All right. Let's do this now then, huh?

02:59.179 --> 03:00.847
You want this, right? Huh?

03:00.930 --> 03:02.390
So, where're you going to stab me?

03:02.473 --> 03:03.975
-[screams]
-[Seon-a] Please!

03:04.058 --> 03:05.059
[objects clattering]

03:06.853 --> 03:08.688
[Dong-eun] If only I had a friend

03:08.771 --> 03:10.481
-[woman] Don't touch Seon-a.
-…or even a god.

03:10.565 --> 03:12.483
-[man scoffs]
-You bastard.

03:12.567 --> 03:15.528
Or the weather could change for me,
just for a second.

03:16.196 --> 03:18.740
-[man] Why don't we all die here?
-And I could have a weapon.

03:18.823 --> 03:20.825
[sounds of struggle continue]

03:23.203 --> 03:26.623
LOOKING FOR A FEMALE WORKER
PLEASE CONTACT ME

03:35.924 --> 03:36.925
[grunts]

03:41.012 --> 03:42.013
[car beeps]

03:42.096 --> 03:45.475
SEOUL JOO GENERAL HOSPITAL

03:53.441 --> 03:55.443
[medical monitors beeping]

03:58.780 --> 04:00.365
I gave you 12 stitches in all.

04:00.448 --> 04:03.785
I'm gonna prescribe you antibiotics,
so no drinking or smoking.

04:03.868 --> 04:04.953
Come on, I'm in high school.

04:05.036 --> 04:07.121
Yeah, you're right. So don't start now.

04:07.997 --> 04:09.374
Come back every three days.

04:09.457 --> 04:11.751
Yeo-jeong, the attending's on his rounds.

04:11.834 --> 04:12.669
Got it.

04:16.297 --> 04:17.257
[man] Hey, Ms. Kim.

04:17.757 --> 04:20.885
Can I have a tiny sip
of what you're drinking?

04:20.969 --> 04:22.595
-My coffee, you mean?
-Don't give him any.

04:23.263 --> 04:25.139
Make sure he doesn't
go near the vending machine.

04:25.723 --> 04:26.766
Yeah.

04:27.934 --> 04:31.479
[man] Has anyone told this man
it's better to eat while you're alive?

04:31.562 --> 04:32.647
Jesus Christ.

04:44.826 --> 04:46.369
LEE SE-DOL 0 VS ALPHAGO 3

04:46.452 --> 04:47.870
FIVE YEARS AFTER THE DUEL

04:49.706 --> 04:51.958
[Dong-eun] Lee Se-dol? Who is that?

04:53.918 --> 04:55.545
[wistful music playing]

04:56.337 --> 04:59.257
Thank you so much for helping me.

04:59.841 --> 05:01.426
You're going to be a great doctor.

05:01.926 --> 05:03.261
Am I not seeing you again?

05:04.887 --> 05:05.972
Wait, why?

05:06.472 --> 05:08.725
I need to keep tutoring you.
You haven't beaten me yet.

05:08.808 --> 05:10.143
[chuckles drily]

05:10.226 --> 05:13.896
You're not the person
I'm actually trying to beat.

05:16.733 --> 05:19.944
I have to get going.
I should go tutor now.

05:23.323 --> 05:25.325
Are you tutoring to save up for a house?

05:25.825 --> 05:27.577
Tutoring isn't enough for that.

05:28.369 --> 05:30.330
You're right.
You almost have to inherit one.

05:31.831 --> 05:32.665
But even still,

05:32.749 --> 05:36.044
how can you be
okay with goodbye after all this?

05:37.712 --> 05:40.089
Just let me know, okay?
Whatever direction you're going.

05:42.842 --> 05:43.843
I know.

05:44.844 --> 05:46.346
You're trying to run away.

05:46.429 --> 05:48.848
Even as we stand here,
you're still running away.

05:50.058 --> 05:51.809
But I don't know
the place you're running to.

05:53.269 --> 05:55.313
If I'm being honest, I also want to…

05:56.981 --> 05:57.940
go run somewhere.

05:58.441 --> 06:00.026
But I'm terrible at directions.

06:02.695 --> 06:04.697
Isn't your mother the hospital chief?

06:05.198 --> 06:06.949
Over at Seoul Joo General Hospital?

06:07.533 --> 06:09.827
[scoffs] Haven't you arrived?

06:10.953 --> 06:12.372
Ever since you were born,

06:12.455 --> 06:15.875
the people around you would tell
this is what you're destined to be,

06:16.918 --> 06:18.419
more times than you can count.

06:21.839 --> 06:24.425
Every single morning,
I watch the weather channel.

06:25.009 --> 06:27.178
When they refer to a winter
that's warmer than usual,

06:27.261 --> 06:28.846
they call it a disturbance.

06:29.889 --> 06:31.599
But thick fog is created

06:32.725 --> 06:35.061
if the disturbance follows
a cold wave during the winter.

06:37.730 --> 06:39.524
Since they stay where it's warm,

06:41.567 --> 06:43.694
they don't realize how cold it is outside.

06:44.946 --> 06:48.366
Life is peaceful and wonderful.

07:15.643 --> 07:16.477
[phone chimes]

07:19.188 --> 07:22.984
GYODAE CAFE

07:25.778 --> 07:28.698
[woman] Where do you want to meet?
Just give me a location.

07:39.917 --> 07:40.918
[paper rustling]

07:54.056 --> 07:55.349
LEE SEOK-JAE

08:05.401 --> 08:07.987
Some basic info is written
on the back of the photo.

08:08.070 --> 08:10.406
I've included everything
I've collected so far.

08:10.990 --> 08:13.367
What I want is
any information that's not there.

08:14.076 --> 08:16.913
That includes anything
regarding Chairman Kim Sin-tae.

08:17.413 --> 08:18.247
Sure…

08:20.958 --> 08:22.293
I'll work eight hours a day.

08:22.376 --> 08:24.253
You can also just pay me minimum wage.

08:24.795 --> 08:27.381
Anything other than that
should be paid to me separately.

08:28.341 --> 08:29.175
Fine.

08:30.510 --> 08:32.512
But be aware,
not everything we do will be legal.

08:33.429 --> 08:35.389
And my business will always come first.

08:36.724 --> 08:37.558
Yeah…

08:38.476 --> 08:41.020
This sort of thing will take some time,

08:41.103 --> 08:43.314
but this way,
we won't get any blood on our hands.

08:45.691 --> 08:46.526
Yeah.

08:48.945 --> 08:50.363
Also, do you know how to drive?

08:51.614 --> 08:52.532
I don't.

08:53.616 --> 08:55.201
Then first, learn how to drive.

08:56.118 --> 08:56.953
Right.

08:59.121 --> 09:01.332
Your daughter.
Tell me, what grade is she in?

09:03.209 --> 09:05.836
Ah, my daughter isn't
going to be any trouble at all.

09:05.920 --> 09:08.047
She can handle herself. She's so grown up.

09:08.130 --> 09:10.216
You don't have to worry about her. I'll--

09:10.299 --> 09:12.718
On the weekends,
send her to the Seoul Station

09:12.802 --> 09:13.928
on a two-hour train ride.

09:14.011 --> 09:14.845
I will tutor her.

09:16.055 --> 09:19.141
And you should also pay me
the same wage for tutoring her.

09:19.225 --> 09:21.727
[lively, spirited music playing]

09:21.811 --> 09:23.062
Thank you, ma'am.

09:24.480 --> 09:26.440
I'll bring back some good news for you.

09:33.906 --> 09:38.995
ON-ROAD DRIVING LESSON
IN PROGRESS

09:39.078 --> 09:40.079
[tires screech]

09:43.124 --> 09:44.125
I'm so sorry.

09:44.917 --> 09:46.335
[alert chimes]

09:46.419 --> 09:48.379
I thought I had hit the brakes.

09:48.462 --> 09:49.714
[car] …and drive forward.

10:02.935 --> 10:06.772
SEMYEONG

10:20.369 --> 10:22.288
MIDDLE SCHOOL MATHEMATICS

10:28.461 --> 10:30.129
How far did we get last time?

10:30.212 --> 10:33.883
Isn't it illegal for a teacher to get paid
for tutoring outside of school?

10:33.966 --> 10:35.217
It is illegal.

10:35.301 --> 10:37.720
But I never was a law-abiding citizen.

10:37.803 --> 10:39.805
[lively, spirited music playing]

10:43.893 --> 10:45.311
DRIVER'S LICENSE
KANG HYEON-NAM

10:46.771 --> 10:48.898
[Hyeon-nam giggling excitedly]

10:52.735 --> 10:53.944
[car beeps]

10:58.115 --> 10:58.949
[gasps]

11:02.828 --> 11:03.746
[exclaims]

11:03.829 --> 11:04.872
Oh my God!

11:05.665 --> 11:06.499
Oh, thank you!

11:06.582 --> 11:08.668
[excited laughter]

11:11.128 --> 11:13.214
Have you used a digital camera before?

11:13.964 --> 11:14.965
[music trails off]

11:16.926 --> 11:17.927
[car beeps]

11:21.222 --> 11:23.641
This rectangular thing
is called an SD card.

11:23.724 --> 11:25.685
I'll give you several of these things.

11:25.768 --> 11:26.602
It goes in…

11:28.646 --> 11:29.730
with a click.

11:29.814 --> 11:31.023
Then you take a picture.

11:31.732 --> 11:35.069
To get it out, press on this and click.
It'll come out.

11:35.152 --> 11:39.156
Then you can leave it right in here
and I'll just come and get it.

11:39.949 --> 11:40.950
Do you understand?

11:42.243 --> 11:43.703
When should I give you the pictures?

11:46.455 --> 11:47.540
They're all in here.

11:48.416 --> 11:50.042
-Oh!
-Here. Try it.

11:53.504 --> 11:54.964
There's so much I have to learn.

11:56.215 --> 11:58.718
Oh, I feel like
I'm going to break this thing.

11:58.801 --> 12:01.137
Yeah, if you try
to put it in there like that.

12:02.596 --> 12:05.141
Make sure that the gold part
goes in first.

12:06.475 --> 12:07.476
[Hyeon-nam sighs]

12:14.316 --> 12:15.317
Got it.

12:23.159 --> 12:24.118
I can't see what…

12:25.870 --> 12:26.871
Oh!

12:27.455 --> 12:28.956
[shutter snapping]

12:30.416 --> 12:32.418
[Dong-eun] Sometimes I wonder, Yeon-jin.

12:33.377 --> 12:34.420
[shutter snapping]

12:34.503 --> 12:36.005
Which of the two is stronger?

12:37.590 --> 12:39.425
The solidarity between victims?

12:40.801 --> 12:43.888
Or the solidarity
between the perpetrators?

12:53.522 --> 12:59.528
[singing in Korean] ♪ Then sings my soul
My Savior God, to Thee ♪

13:00.112 --> 13:06.619
♪ How great Thou art ♪

13:06.702 --> 13:13.125
♪ Then sings my soul
My Savior God, to Thee ♪

13:13.209 --> 13:20.174
♪ How great Thou art ♪

13:21.842 --> 13:23.928
♪ When through the woods… ♪

13:43.906 --> 13:44.907
[car beeps]

13:56.627 --> 14:00.047
[Hyeon-nam in English] My pictures
don't look that great yet. Sorry.

14:00.130 --> 14:02.800
I thought you might recognize her anyway.

14:09.682 --> 14:10.599
[tablet chimes]

14:22.486 --> 14:25.322
RAINBOW EYE CLINIC

14:26.282 --> 14:28.284
[mysterious, suspenseful music playing]

14:30.286 --> 14:33.914
RAINBOW EYE CLINIC

14:42.548 --> 14:43.632
DR. GLASSES (CONTACTS)

14:43.716 --> 14:47.219
CORNEAL DISEASE, COLOR BLINDNESS
CORRECTIVE LENS STORE

14:48.178 --> 14:49.555
[blows landing]

14:51.307 --> 14:53.309
[students murmuring]

14:53.392 --> 14:54.935
[boy 1 grunting]

15:00.232 --> 15:01.233
[boy 2 exclaiming]

15:03.277 --> 15:04.278
Say that again.

15:04.945 --> 15:07.698
You couldn't shut up about it before,
so why're you quiet now?

15:07.781 --> 15:10.951
What'd you say about my eyes?
The hell you say, fucker?

15:23.047 --> 15:24.173
What color is this, then?

15:25.007 --> 15:26.926
Tell me what color it is right now!

15:31.931 --> 15:33.515
He's knocked out. You can stop.

15:35.643 --> 15:39.104
You fucking pussy.
I'm colorblind, but I'm not blind!

15:39.188 --> 15:40.981
I know that I knocked him out!

15:45.694 --> 15:48.781
[Dong-eun] Looks like
you weren't a very loyal wife, Yeon-jin.

15:49.615 --> 15:52.117
However, you try your best to hide it.

15:56.830 --> 15:59.083
[woman] I told her it was
too dangerous to play with those.

15:59.166 --> 16:00.167
Oh, it's fine.

16:00.250 --> 16:03.295
Wow, Ye-sol! You've gotten so tall!

16:03.379 --> 16:06.799
Yeah! I'm going to be
a forecaster like you!

16:07.299 --> 16:09.802
This has been Ha Ye-sol
reporting the weather.

16:09.885 --> 16:13.222
Hey, Mommy, are these heels green?

16:15.808 --> 16:18.018
Oh… they're actually red.

16:19.895 --> 16:21.981
Ha Ye-sol, look at Mommy.

16:22.648 --> 16:25.818
The color of these heels
does not matter at all.

16:25.901 --> 16:29.905
What's important is that they cost a lot,
and they're real hard to get.

16:30.656 --> 16:33.701
And what's even more important
is that no matter how rare,

16:33.784 --> 16:35.744
you can own each and every one of them.

16:36.412 --> 16:39.748
The true value of something is
the number written on its price tag.

16:39.832 --> 16:41.000
Not its colors, honey.

16:41.709 --> 16:42.793
Do you understand me?

16:44.712 --> 16:46.672
And I shouldn't tell Daddy, right?

16:57.016 --> 16:58.517
[woman] Oh! Jae-jun, hey!

16:59.768 --> 17:01.437
Here comes the owner of the club.

17:01.937 --> 17:05.607
Wow! Look who we have over here!
It's been too long.

17:06.442 --> 17:07.776
-Hola!
-Hola.

17:09.028 --> 17:12.740
Ah, senorita. As beautiful as always.

17:12.823 --> 17:16.744
[chuckles] If you would've called before,
I would've rolled out the red carpet.

17:16.827 --> 17:18.662
Ah, sure you would.

17:19.705 --> 17:23.042
When we were in Spain, we were
next door neighbors to Jae-jun here.

17:23.542 --> 17:27.129
Ah, I'd like my friend to meet you.
I want her to be a member.

17:27.212 --> 17:29.173
-Mmm.
-Consider it for me? Please?

17:29.256 --> 17:30.382
Dramatic much?

17:31.091 --> 17:33.969
Do I need to be considered
if we know I can afford it?

17:34.887 --> 17:36.096
Have you enjoyed yourself?

17:36.597 --> 17:39.016
Our country club has the best
golfing greens in the country.

17:39.099 --> 17:41.185
There are some people
who have never been here,

17:41.268 --> 17:42.519
but none only come once.

17:43.103 --> 17:44.688
Exercise anywhere is great.

17:45.189 --> 17:46.565
I did like the dumplings here.

17:47.608 --> 17:49.610
It's really hard to get a spot in here.

17:50.110 --> 17:53.363
Four current members
need to recommend you before submission.

17:53.864 --> 17:56.950
-I swear. She is everything you want.
-Huh.

17:57.034 --> 17:59.620
Her son is the CEO
of Jaepyeong Construction.

17:59.703 --> 18:02.164
[tense, mysterious music playing]

18:07.669 --> 18:10.881
[chuckles] If you give it to me,
I'll personally review it.

18:11.632 --> 18:13.717
Sorry. I've gotta get going.

18:14.384 --> 18:16.136
-I'll call you later.
-Sure, thanks!

18:19.431 --> 18:22.351
Don't accept any applications.
I'm not accepting new members.

18:22.434 --> 18:23.435
Oh, and…

18:25.687 --> 18:26.688
[sighs angrily]

18:28.315 --> 18:29.733
…don't sell dumplings there.

18:29.817 --> 18:31.610
Throw that fucking shit out.

18:32.653 --> 18:33.821
[man] Yes. Got it, sir.

18:38.826 --> 18:40.869
PAGODA GO CLUB

18:58.637 --> 19:01.723
Park the car. Give the keys
to the Go house. Take the weekend.

19:02.432 --> 19:03.851
Thank you. Have a good night, sir.

19:03.934 --> 19:05.435
Mr. Choi is waiting for you.

19:05.519 --> 19:07.771
Hmm. Thank you.

19:12.609 --> 19:16.738
For the Jeongbok-dong development,
I've secured the land rights for you.

19:18.240 --> 19:21.660
And I've reached
an agreement with the city

19:21.743 --> 19:24.454
to open the Go square as soon as possible.

19:24.538 --> 19:26.874
I guess changing the company
slowed us down.

19:29.710 --> 19:31.253
[indistinct chatter]

19:34.256 --> 19:36.925
You know, most young people

19:37.009 --> 19:39.678
aren't very interested in things like Go.

19:39.761 --> 19:41.763
[chuckles] You don't see that often.

19:42.848 --> 19:45.017
If you look over there, Mr. Park,

19:45.100 --> 19:49.021
the owner of the ribs restaurant
is absolutely fuming

19:49.104 --> 19:51.148
because he's lost two rounds in a row.

19:51.231 --> 19:54.693
They're betting 20,000 won per round.

19:55.194 --> 19:56.195
Really?

20:01.450 --> 20:03.994
How'd you even catch that?
He went down by…

20:04.077 --> 20:05.913
[tense music playing]

20:10.250 --> 20:12.252
[bystanders mutter]

20:15.172 --> 20:17.382
[man] You have to get
the group there first.

20:20.969 --> 20:22.804
You won't find any help over there.

20:22.888 --> 20:24.806
Give up and you'll only lose
by ten territories.

20:28.936 --> 20:30.187
[player sighs in frustration]

20:31.605 --> 20:33.815
-Hmm.
-[bystander] Wow, she's good.

20:36.777 --> 20:37.861
[player] Goddamn.

20:37.945 --> 20:38.946
Got him good here.

20:39.821 --> 20:42.157
[player] Ugh, I can't believe it.

20:43.825 --> 20:46.161
[bystander] Wow, that's impressive.
Very impressive.

20:50.374 --> 20:53.043
Wow, she's very good. Incredible.

21:19.278 --> 21:21.280
[mysterious music playing]

21:29.037 --> 21:29.871
JAE-JUN

21:29.955 --> 21:32.916
I'm in Seoul right now.
Tomorrow, I'm off and I'm bored.

21:36.378 --> 21:39.423
[bright, upbeat music playing]

21:40.966 --> 21:42.551
Oops. Wrong number.

21:44.761 --> 21:45.887
[car honks]

21:52.644 --> 21:54.396
Is he insane?

22:00.652 --> 22:01.737
[music stops]

22:03.196 --> 22:04.197
[chuckles]

22:06.616 --> 22:08.452
You smiling because
you thought I was Jae-jun?

22:08.535 --> 22:11.246
Shit… that's fucking funny. [laughs]

22:11.330 --> 22:12.789
Just open the door now!

22:22.716 --> 22:24.634
[Myeong-o] You picked
a good one this time.

22:26.303 --> 22:27.471
iPad's in the back.

22:32.684 --> 22:35.270
Are you allowed
to drive Jae-jun's car whenever?

22:35.354 --> 22:37.356
I bet you say it's yours to pick up women.

22:37.439 --> 22:39.900
Without some perks,
this job would be shit.

22:41.193 --> 22:42.194
Six. Nine.

22:43.820 --> 22:45.322
Six. Nine. Six. Nine.

22:46.031 --> 22:47.199
The password.

22:48.867 --> 22:52.287
-What a number, huh?
-Ugh. So gross.

22:53.663 --> 22:54.915
He just got a divorce,

22:55.415 --> 22:57.751
and he owns a ton of property and shit.

22:57.834 --> 22:59.419
He even owns horses in Jeju.

22:59.503 --> 23:03.382
Oh! Oh my God, I thought he was joking.

23:03.465 --> 23:04.841
Fuck me.

23:07.219 --> 23:10.222
Can you find out a little bit more
about this guy's ex-wife?

23:10.722 --> 23:13.225
What she looks like. Family. Anything.

23:13.308 --> 23:15.685
For 300,000 won, how long would it take?

23:15.769 --> 23:17.396
What's the rush here?

23:17.479 --> 23:20.690
Four hundred fifty thousand won.
I'm a busy man nowadays.

23:20.774 --> 23:23.110
He wants to go to Jeju with me soon.

23:23.193 --> 23:25.070
I have to decide
if I'm sleeping with him or not.

23:25.153 --> 23:27.072
Ah!

23:27.155 --> 23:30.325
Of course you have to.
I'm sorry, all right?

23:30.409 --> 23:33.328
[chuckles] Gotta make sure.

23:33.412 --> 23:35.080
What a slut. Oh God.

23:35.163 --> 23:36.581
[scoffs] Shit.

23:36.665 --> 23:38.166
You're not worth cussing out.

23:38.250 --> 23:42.254
Do you know the one place
where class distinction is crystal clear?

23:42.921 --> 23:44.172
It's in a plane.

23:44.256 --> 23:47.175
First class, business, economy.

23:47.259 --> 23:49.386
While the only thing
dividing them is a curtain,

23:49.469 --> 23:50.637
no one's allowed to cross it.

23:50.720 --> 23:52.139
The hell you saying?

23:52.931 --> 23:55.559
I'm saying people like yourself
will never be allowed to cross it.

23:55.642 --> 23:58.270
You're not getting paid enough
to buy a proper meal.

23:58.770 --> 23:59.771
But I will.

24:00.272 --> 24:01.857
[menacing music plays]

24:01.940 --> 24:02.983
Stop the car.

24:03.066 --> 24:04.985
Well, Jae-jun's car.

24:10.365 --> 24:11.366
[music halts]

24:17.247 --> 24:18.957
[introspective music playing]

24:44.065 --> 24:45.233
Still playing with that?

24:46.193 --> 24:49.905
The match was already over,
but she dragged it out.

24:49.988 --> 24:51.114
Why, though?

24:51.698 --> 24:52.616
Who did?

24:53.200 --> 24:54.159
At the Go house.

24:56.411 --> 24:57.245
What?

24:58.330 --> 25:00.790
I'm going to rest for a bit,
then I'm off to work.

25:02.501 --> 25:05.128
That thing gives me such a headache.
How can you play it?

25:05.212 --> 25:06.963
It can be a pretty compelling game.

25:07.964 --> 25:10.050
Why do you smoke
even though it's not good for you?

25:10.133 --> 25:11.051
Got it.

25:11.885 --> 25:14.596
Then, why did you marry a woman who smokes

25:14.679 --> 25:16.014
when you yourself don't smoke?

25:16.097 --> 25:18.183
Aside from smoking, you're compelling.

25:18.683 --> 25:21.561
Both for fun and to look at.

25:22.062 --> 25:25.440
[Yeon-jin laughs]
That's what I like about you, sweetie.

25:25.524 --> 25:27.776
You answer every question I ask you.

25:28.860 --> 25:33.114
I wonder, you went on blind dates
with at least three women, including me.

25:33.698 --> 25:34.699
Why was I picked?

25:34.783 --> 25:36.910
You had the least amount of clothing on.

25:37.410 --> 25:40.747
And though you were
wearing the least, it was all Dior.

25:40.830 --> 25:42.374
[laughs]

25:42.457 --> 25:44.042
You're so out of your mind.

25:44.876 --> 25:48.129
For such a nice boy,
you sure can act like a real bad guy.

25:50.382 --> 25:52.050
Hurry up, Do-yeong.

25:52.592 --> 25:55.845
There's very, very little
I'm wearing tonight.

25:56.638 --> 25:57.472
Five minutes.

26:04.563 --> 26:05.897
[train horn blares]

26:05.981 --> 26:08.858
[PA system chimes]

26:08.942 --> 26:10.902
[announcer over PA]
May I have your attention?

26:10.986 --> 26:12.779
In the interest of safety,

26:12.862 --> 26:15.907
please stand behind the platform
as the train approaches.

26:15.991 --> 26:17.576
The train will now be approaching.

26:39.973 --> 26:43.101
[gentle music playing]

26:48.982 --> 26:49.899
Are you real?

26:51.943 --> 26:53.153
What do you mean?

26:54.696 --> 26:55.614
I dressed up.

27:01.161 --> 27:01.995
[phone chimes]

27:03.496 --> 27:05.165
[Dong-eun] We'll start in ten minutes.

27:06.708 --> 27:08.793
[gentle music continuing]

27:08.877 --> 27:10.962
[Yeo-jeong] Did you pass your exam?

27:12.047 --> 27:14.382
-Yeah.
-Ah. Of course you did.

27:15.592 --> 27:16.676
Congrats.

27:18.219 --> 27:19.679
Ah, I might be too late.

27:20.722 --> 27:21.723
Thank you.

27:28.772 --> 27:32.108
Semyeong was hosting a conference,
and I went with some professors.

27:36.863 --> 27:38.198
Have you been well?

27:39.074 --> 27:39.908
Kind of.

27:40.992 --> 27:43.328
I heard you went into the military
as a medic.

27:43.411 --> 27:46.122
Yeah, but it's been forever
since I've been discharged.

27:47.082 --> 27:48.291
But how did you know?

27:49.542 --> 27:51.169
From those old guys at the park.

27:52.253 --> 27:54.839
They said the lazy kid went to go serve,

27:54.923 --> 27:56.800
and that he'd come back a new man.

28:00.929 --> 28:02.847
So you kept going to the park, then?

28:05.850 --> 28:08.103
Did you want me
to write you a letter or something?

28:08.186 --> 28:09.771
Are medics even allowed to get letters?

28:11.147 --> 28:14.150
-They usually get a lot of love letters.
-Did you get a lot then?

28:20.323 --> 28:21.449
TO JOO YEO-JEONG

28:21.533 --> 28:23.451
FROM CHEONGSONG PRISON

28:24.160 --> 28:25.161
Not big on letters.

28:27.372 --> 28:29.290
So, what brings you to Semyeong?

28:30.041 --> 28:31.126
Are you working there now?

28:31.876 --> 28:32.711
Not yet, no.

28:33.294 --> 28:35.463
I had some business there.

28:38.049 --> 28:38.883
Is she with you?

28:39.676 --> 28:41.344
She's been staring at you for a while now.

28:43.555 --> 28:45.181
I probably should get going now.

28:49.060 --> 28:49.894
Me too.

28:50.729 --> 28:52.021
And by the way…

28:54.023 --> 28:54.899
back then,

28:55.817 --> 28:58.194
when we were
playing Go together at the park,

28:59.320 --> 29:03.575
I was going through
the coldest season in my whole life.

29:06.244 --> 29:07.912
But when we were playing Go…

29:10.665 --> 29:14.169
that was the only thing
in my life that kept me warm.

29:16.045 --> 29:18.173
So if you think
that I might have a kind heart,

29:19.549 --> 29:21.134
then you're the one to thank.

29:22.802 --> 29:24.679
[heartfelt music playing]

29:24.763 --> 29:26.181
Just wanted you to know.

29:36.941 --> 29:38.151
That's where I work now.

29:39.110 --> 29:40.862
Just in case you're ready one day.

29:44.657 --> 29:45.784
Have a safe trip.

29:56.544 --> 30:01.132
SEOUL JOO GENERAL HOSPITAL
PLASTIC SURGEON JOO YEO-JEONG

30:12.143 --> 30:13.228
[woman] Excuse me.

30:15.647 --> 30:17.565
EDEN APARTMENTS

30:17.649 --> 30:19.818
Is this your main residence?

30:19.901 --> 30:21.611
You live in 301, right?

30:21.694 --> 30:24.197
You should know I own this building.

30:25.365 --> 30:26.616
I'm aware of that, ma'am.

30:27.116 --> 30:29.202
Do you not live in your apartment?

30:29.285 --> 30:31.955
Your utility bills are
always the lowest here.

30:33.206 --> 30:36.209
-I always pay my rent on time though.
-And I know that, dear.

30:36.876 --> 30:40.255
I was just wondering
what was going on in there.

30:40.338 --> 30:42.298
You were so desperate to live here,

30:42.382 --> 30:45.009
but you've been
leaving it empty for months now.

30:46.010 --> 30:48.680
I haven't been sent to Semyeong just yet.

30:49.264 --> 30:50.265
But I'm trying my best.

30:55.770 --> 30:58.189
[Hyeon-nam] I know
we're not supposed to meet in person,

30:58.273 --> 30:59.774
but I have a video to show you.

30:59.858 --> 31:01.276
So I'll meet you in the car.

31:01.943 --> 31:03.111
[door opens]

31:05.488 --> 31:07.323
I thought you were
coming in from the front.

31:07.407 --> 31:10.577
Ah! I'm so sorry. Got it.
I'll remember this next time.

31:12.453 --> 31:15.373
I had to zoom in a ton to get it,
so the quality isn't great.

31:15.456 --> 31:16.916
You'll need to look closely.

31:17.625 --> 31:18.626
-Here.
-Thanks.

31:29.846 --> 31:32.682
There. There. There, you see?
You see? Just look.

31:37.604 --> 31:38.938
-Here.
-[camera beeps]

31:43.401 --> 31:47.071
"Hey, sir. Why don't you
sit up front with me today?"

31:50.950 --> 31:52.702
-I'm not sure what this is.
-[sighs]

31:57.707 --> 32:00.877
"Hey, baby.
Sit up front with me. Come on."

32:07.175 --> 32:09.010
Wait, was the driver's name Jo Su-hyeon?

32:09.093 --> 32:10.595
[gasps] How did you know?

32:11.179 --> 32:12.931
[sighs] It was never a woman.

32:13.014 --> 32:14.015
Uh-huh.

32:14.724 --> 32:17.435
There was a box
of erectile dysfunction medication.

32:17.518 --> 32:21.022
I guess gender doesn't matter
as long as you last.

32:22.065 --> 32:24.150
So we should have focused on the age.

32:24.233 --> 32:25.234
[laughs]

32:26.945 --> 32:30.198
Sorry. You get so serious
at the weirdest times.

32:33.826 --> 32:34.827
[stops laughing]

32:35.536 --> 32:36.746
What's wrong?

32:36.829 --> 32:39.832
Did you think I couldn't laugh
because my husband beats me?

32:41.084 --> 32:43.294
I might get hit, but I'm a happy person.

32:43.378 --> 32:44.963
Oh Jesus.

32:50.176 --> 32:52.512
You should have
told me about that earlier.

32:53.346 --> 32:55.348
-Tell what?
-That you're a happy person.

32:56.724 --> 32:58.351
You see, I don't want to laugh with you.

32:58.851 --> 33:00.311
Why… Why not?

33:03.481 --> 33:06.150
I'm afraid I'll forget
what I'm supposed to be doing

33:06.234 --> 33:07.485
if I let myself laugh.

33:09.696 --> 33:12.991
Ah, I'm sorry. I didn't know that.

33:14.409 --> 33:15.410
I'll be careful.

33:17.161 --> 33:18.955
Maybe this is why I get beaten up.

33:19.038 --> 33:20.415
Don't say that.

33:29.132 --> 33:31.801
Well, I guess I just really love
working with you.

33:32.301 --> 33:35.221
I'm a happy person
who never gets to be happy.

33:35.304 --> 33:37.974
I can breathe now, so I can't stop now.

33:42.603 --> 33:45.523
Don't worry, ma'am.
I'll make sure not to bother you.

33:46.149 --> 33:47.859
Well, let's go!

33:50.111 --> 33:51.571
[sweeping choral music plays]

33:51.654 --> 33:53.740
[Dong-eun] How come she and I…

33:53.823 --> 33:58.369
No, how come we have to
work so hard every day?

33:59.454 --> 34:01.956
Working hard is so tiring.

34:03.166 --> 34:05.251
I'm so sick of working hard, Yeon-jin.

34:05.334 --> 34:06.335
[woman] It's ready, miss.

34:15.011 --> 34:16.012
[doorbell rings]

34:18.181 --> 34:19.515
[door opens]

34:23.728 --> 34:25.146
How have you been, Mr. Kim?

34:25.646 --> 34:27.148
I'm Moon Dong-eun.

34:29.025 --> 34:30.026
You're who?

34:30.610 --> 34:31.944
From Seonghan High School.

34:32.445 --> 34:35.490
The Dong-eun who dropped out
back then in 2004.

34:35.573 --> 34:36.908
Don't you remember me?

34:39.660 --> 34:41.662
[hesitating] Who are you?

34:47.126 --> 34:48.753
Oh, hi, Su-han.

34:48.836 --> 34:51.881
It's nice seeing you.
What brings you to this neighborhood?

34:52.465 --> 34:54.509
Dong-eun? What are you doing here?

34:54.592 --> 34:57.053
This is my dad's house. He's my father.

34:57.136 --> 34:58.638
Oh, is that so?

34:59.222 --> 35:01.974
Wow. This must be fate, then.

35:02.058 --> 35:04.352
I used to be
a student of your father's, long ago.

35:07.980 --> 35:09.273
Right? Don't you remember me now?

35:10.358 --> 35:14.737
Oh, almost forgot, Mr. Kim.
Now, I'm a teacher like you.

35:19.659 --> 35:21.953
What'd you say about…

35:23.079 --> 35:24.413
my son?!

35:24.497 --> 35:27.125
-Say it again? What?!
-[blows landing]

35:27.208 --> 35:29.710
[menacing music playing]

35:47.311 --> 35:50.481
Why'd you wanna meet here?
Siesta would've been better.

35:52.608 --> 35:55.778
Did you know that even in high school,
this building was abandoned?

35:56.279 --> 35:57.405
And it still is today.

35:57.488 --> 35:59.198
Enough with the small talk.

36:00.825 --> 36:03.536
You're trying to get revenge here,
aren't you?

36:04.120 --> 36:04.954
Yeah. I am.

36:05.037 --> 36:05.955
Wow.

36:06.038 --> 36:07.957
You don't even seem scared of me, huh?

36:08.791 --> 36:10.376
Why aren't you after me, then?

36:12.170 --> 36:14.589
I can't get revenge on you
if you have nothing.

36:14.672 --> 36:16.632
All the others have something to lose.

36:16.716 --> 36:18.843
You have nothing to lose.

36:18.926 --> 36:21.304
Wow, you'd say that to my face? [chuckles]

36:22.054 --> 36:25.683
This is the perfect height
to fall and die. Watch your mouth.

36:27.894 --> 36:28.728
I know.

36:29.937 --> 36:31.689
I stood on that ledge once myself.

36:32.690 --> 36:35.610
-Because of you guys.
-Shit, are you threatening me?

36:37.987 --> 36:41.199
-At least you can get scared.
-You really are asking for it, aren't you?

36:45.786 --> 36:48.206
-Remember Yoon So-hee?
-What?

36:48.289 --> 36:50.458
So many rumors were
going around about her.

36:50.541 --> 36:52.877
About how she killed herself
after she left.

36:52.960 --> 36:54.712
You should remember that at least.

36:54.795 --> 36:56.672
You used to say "Dong-eun's here,"

36:56.756 --> 37:01.010
but you probably said "So-hee's here"
before that.

37:01.093 --> 37:03.095
[suspenseful music playing]

37:07.892 --> 37:10.061
So-hee fell from this exact place.

37:11.020 --> 37:12.313
But she was pushed.

37:12.396 --> 37:13.397
[loud clatter]

37:22.823 --> 37:25.826
What the hell? No! No! Not me, huh?

37:25.910 --> 37:27.078
I wasn't the one!

37:27.161 --> 37:28.162
I know.

37:29.372 --> 37:32.124
So go get some money
from the person who actually killed her.

37:32.625 --> 37:34.126
I have the info you want.

37:39.715 --> 37:41.050
Well, who was it, then?

37:42.468 --> 37:45.137
I told you. My business
comes first and foremost.

37:51.352 --> 37:54.146
There was so much fucking dog hair,
but I got them.

37:55.523 --> 37:57.358
Ten, with the roots attached, right?

37:57.441 --> 37:58.276
So, hey,

37:59.318 --> 38:03.281
did you… have Jae-jun's kid or something?

38:04.115 --> 38:05.199
[Dong-eun scoffs]

38:05.283 --> 38:06.784
You'd have his kid before me.

38:08.160 --> 38:09.912
I'll call when I've confirmed this.

38:15.293 --> 38:17.378
[Dong-eun] I didn't forget you, Myeong-o.

38:17.920 --> 38:20.339
Of course you also have something to lose.

38:20.423 --> 38:21.424
Just one thing.

38:22.466 --> 38:23.467
Your life.

38:24.051 --> 38:25.594
[medical monitor beeping]

38:26.512 --> 38:27.513
[door opens]

38:27.596 --> 38:28.973
[footsteps approaching]

38:31.767 --> 38:32.768
[woman sighs]

38:59.920 --> 39:02.757
Do it on her arm, not her hand.
She says it hurts if it's there.

39:02.840 --> 39:05.009
Come on, Sa-ra.
Hurry and wake up to detox.

39:05.092 --> 39:06.385
You need to go to the exhibition.

39:07.094 --> 39:09.347
[Sa-ra moans] It's too bright.

39:10.931 --> 39:12.141
Are you an angel?

39:12.224 --> 39:14.143
Enough. Now hurry and get up.

39:14.935 --> 39:16.812
You have a special exhibition today.

39:16.896 --> 39:18.356
[Sa-ra groans]

39:18.439 --> 39:21.275
If you're gonna smoke, at least
smoke something with a weaker smell.

39:21.359 --> 39:24.945
There are slim cigarettes, you know.
What? Your dealer can't do that?

39:26.489 --> 39:32.370
LEE SA-RA SPECIAL EXHIBITION
GAZING AT AN IDEAL INSIDE A DREAM

39:32.453 --> 39:35.873
[elegant classical music playing]

39:35.956 --> 39:38.209
Hey. I want that one.

39:38.876 --> 39:40.211
Send it straight to the club.

39:40.294 --> 39:42.755
You know shipping's separate,
dear customer?

39:42.838 --> 39:46.675
-Rich ones are always greediest.
-After taxes, I pretty much pay it back.

39:46.759 --> 39:48.469
My talent's basically for charity.

39:48.552 --> 39:50.638
Since you only pay income tax,

39:50.721 --> 39:54.016
you don't know there are
other people in a different tax bracket.

39:54.100 --> 39:55.101
[snickers]

39:55.184 --> 39:56.727
[glass ringing]

39:58.020 --> 39:58.938
[woman] Sa-ra?

39:59.730 --> 40:01.440
Hey, hide my drink.

40:04.527 --> 40:06.320
This is Mrs. Jang,
the wife of Buil's chairman.

40:06.404 --> 40:08.239
Oh, hello!

40:08.322 --> 40:10.699
[Mrs. Jang] These paintings
are stunning, dear.

40:10.783 --> 40:12.576
I wonder how Ms. Lee was blessed

40:12.660 --> 40:15.704
with such incredible talent
from our wonderful Lord.

40:15.788 --> 40:16.622
Amen.

40:17.331 --> 40:18.791
She bought three pieces already.

40:18.874 --> 40:20.334
Oh, thank you, ma'am.

40:21.377 --> 40:22.962
-Please come with me.
-Oh, sure.

40:26.257 --> 40:27.091
[Jae-jun] Wow.

40:27.174 --> 40:30.469
How the hell can you bear
to put up with that? Tell me, Ms. Lee.

40:30.553 --> 40:31.595
[simpering laugh]

40:31.679 --> 40:34.098
So, I'm getting
a fucking funny award next month.

40:34.682 --> 40:37.726
You should come
and get embarrassed with me. [giggles]

40:37.810 --> 40:39.061
You should come too, Ms. Lee.

40:39.145 --> 40:40.896
Stop it right now.

40:42.690 --> 40:45.901
So what award are you getting, hmm?

40:45.985 --> 40:47.486
2022 PROUD ALUMNI AWARDS CEREMONY

40:50.990 --> 40:54.034
[Hye-jeong] Incredible.
This place has hardly changed.

40:54.118 --> 40:55.619
-[line ringing]
-My first time back.

40:55.703 --> 40:58.372
Really? You never saw
the gym teacher again?

40:58.456 --> 41:01.000
Hye-jeong broke up with him.
He was pissed.

41:01.625 --> 41:03.294
-Were you not back in Korea yet?
-Mmm.

41:03.377 --> 41:05.504
Paris, watching Lovers in Paris.

41:05.588 --> 41:08.757
Each episode took four days to download.
Still watched it all though.

41:08.841 --> 41:10.092
Loved it all.

41:10.801 --> 41:12.845
Why isn't this asshole answering?

41:12.928 --> 41:14.305
He has something I need.

41:14.388 --> 41:15.222
Myeong-o?

41:16.223 --> 41:17.808
You can't reach him, also?

41:17.892 --> 41:20.978
Ah, shit I need something from him, too.
No idea where he is?

41:21.061 --> 41:23.230
He probably got drunk
and passed out somewhere.

41:24.773 --> 41:26.317
I should've fired that idiot already.

41:26.901 --> 41:29.236
[footsteps approaching]

41:44.919 --> 41:47.671
[footsteps clacking loudly]

41:54.553 --> 41:57.640
Wow. It's been far too long, you guys.

41:58.349 --> 42:00.017
How's everyone been? [gasps]

42:00.935 --> 42:02.686
I swear I've seen her before.

42:03.479 --> 42:07.983
Wow, it's been forever since the six of us
were all together, huh?

42:08.567 --> 42:11.070
Don't you mean the five of us?
Myeong-o's not here.

42:11.153 --> 42:12.947
Ha! Moon So-hui? That's it.

42:13.781 --> 42:16.242
It's not her.
Moon Dong-eun and Yun So-hui.

42:16.825 --> 42:19.912
I heard after she dropped out,
she went to work in a factory.

42:20.746 --> 42:22.248
What're you doing here now?

42:22.331 --> 42:24.500
You're not an alum, like we are.

42:24.583 --> 42:27.586
Sorry, but I feel bad I can't recall
our fond times with you.

42:27.670 --> 42:29.547
Anyway, it's good seeing you, So-hee!

42:29.630 --> 42:31.215
I told you, it's Dong-eun.

42:32.967 --> 42:35.469
I actually come to this gym
every once in a while.

42:36.470 --> 42:40.307
But it seems today I've got
all my friends together again.

42:40.391 --> 42:41.600
[tense music playing]

42:41.684 --> 42:43.102
How have you been, Yeon-jin?

42:43.602 --> 42:45.437
I love watching your weather reports.

42:46.647 --> 42:50.651
Whenever I watch it,
I think, "You just look so good."

42:55.739 --> 42:56.907
And you?

42:59.994 --> 43:01.579
How have you been doing lately?

43:01.662 --> 43:05.082
I just got a new job,
so I've been pretty busy with that.

43:06.542 --> 43:09.670
Got some new clothes. Ate sashimi too.

43:09.753 --> 43:12.172
[Dong-eun] You're chairman
for the Semyeong school district?

43:12.256 --> 43:13.090
WILL - KIM SHIN-TAE

43:13.173 --> 43:14.466
Congratulations.

43:19.096 --> 43:20.931
And who are you?

43:21.015 --> 43:23.100
Did you dig through my trash to find this?

43:23.183 --> 43:24.810
I'm sorry, but there was no other way.

43:25.686 --> 43:28.355
The name of your driver is
Jo Soo-hyeon, right?

43:29.607 --> 43:33.652
Do your son
and future daughter-in-law know

43:33.736 --> 43:37.615
that their inheritance will be divided
and shared with Jo Su-hyeon as well?

43:38.449 --> 43:41.702
Are you trying
to threaten me right now, woman?

43:41.785 --> 43:43.162
[chuckles drily]

43:43.245 --> 43:44.163
I apologize.

43:44.913 --> 43:47.333
What I need is something
you can do quite easily.

43:47.416 --> 43:50.919
All you have to do is bring me onboard
to teach your first grade's class two.

43:51.837 --> 43:53.505
I'm more than qualified for the position.

43:53.589 --> 43:55.841
Currently, I have
an apartment in Semyeong,

43:55.924 --> 43:58.761
and I have already
submitted my resignation to my school.

43:59.845 --> 44:00.846
Transfer school?

44:01.430 --> 44:02.431
Yeah.

44:03.474 --> 44:07.061
May I start at the beginning
of the new school year?

44:08.854 --> 44:09.855
[birds chirping]

44:25.204 --> 44:28.582
HA YE-SOL

44:28.666 --> 44:31.001
[intricate, suspenseful music playing]

44:31.085 --> 44:33.170
[emcee] Now, we will begin
the award ceremony.

44:33.253 --> 44:38.300
Our first award goes to Park Yeon-jin,
an alumni from the 23rd graduating class.

44:42.096 --> 44:44.390
2022 PROUD ALUMNI AWARDS CEREMONY

44:49.061 --> 44:52.648
From now on,
every single day will be a nightmare.

44:53.357 --> 44:56.068
Each day will be
disturbing and terrifying.

44:56.568 --> 44:59.947
You won't be able to stop me
or make me disappear.

45:00.781 --> 45:06.537
I plan on becoming
a very old rumor of yours, Yeon-jin.

45:14.962 --> 45:16.046
[applause trails off]

45:20.092 --> 45:21.844
Let's give it up for Yeon-jin!

45:22.720 --> 45:24.012
Bravo!

45:24.513 --> 45:26.932
You're so incredible, Yeon-jin! Ah!

45:27.015 --> 45:28.267
Whoo!

45:29.935 --> 45:31.353
[spirited applause]

45:36.191 --> 45:37.901
[low, menacing music builds]

45:39.278 --> 45:41.280
[applause fades away]

45:41.363 --> 45:43.365
[menacing music continues]

45:53.333 --> 45:58.380
[moody pop outro music playing]
